caption: Spawn Traits and the Retention Depth Limit
tradition-component: spawn-traits-and-the-retention-depth-limit

A Spawn Trait is a permanent trait learned from a Power Stunt whose source was a Gift Trait or another Root Trait defined below. A Spawn Trait may itself be used as the source of later Power Stunts, but traits manifested from those stunts cannot be permanently retained through Spawn.

A temporary ability manifested from a Spawn Trait is a Manifestation. A Manifestation may function normally for the duration of the stunt, but it grants no Spawn purchase permission. Spawn never permits a third permanent generation. Another Tradition may independently grant purchase access, but that purchase does not retroactively become part of Spawn's retention chain.

The retention structure is therefore: Gift or Root Trait → retainable Spawn Trait → temporary Manifestation.
